From: KRdp displayless experiment <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Stream one persistent output and change its layout in place

With KRDP_PERSISTENT_OUTPUT naming an output, every connection streams that
existing output instead of creating a virtual monitor of its own. Its mode and
scale are set to the client's on connect, and again whenever the client sends a
Display Control layout, through the output-lifecycle helper's "prepare" action.
After each layout the stream is asked for the new size too: KWin 6.8 does not
resize a stream from a virtual output when the output's mode changes, so the
client would keep getting frames of the old size. Disconnecting changes
nothing, so a reconnect with the same geometry causes no relayout, and a new
connection never waits for the previous one to tear down.

Display Control now accepts multi-monitor layouts, following the client's
primary monitor, and carries the client's scale with the size.
